Z||000006||ChadMan||06-08-2001||09:13 AM||||I bought Amnesiac yesterday.  I'm a little disappointed...it's a LOT like Kid A."  To me, they're both "music as art" albums that you listen to a few times, appreciate, and put back on your CD shelf.<P>OK Computer was such a masterpiece that I wonder if they can ever make something that brilliant again.  Seems like they're doing the "Icarus-too-close-to-the-sun" thing now.<P>I guess I shouldn't complain...Radiohead makes music for themselves, not for the general public.  If they worried about pleasing critics and listeners, they'd wake up one day and be the Backside Boys.<P>By the way, Eric, I understood your post to mean you are waiting to buy Amnesiac because you didn't like Kid A, and because you heard Amnesiac wasn't like OK Computer.  Then you listened to OK Computer again and thought it was still pretty freakin' good.  Am I right?||||reg||9
Z||000007||Eric||06-08-2001||09:26 AM||||Yes, sir.  That's what I meant.  Maybe JohnnyK doesn't know much about Radiohead.  Too bad the CD is not like previous albums.||||reg||1
Z||000008||turbo86se||06-08-2001||12:12 PM||||I'm not a huge Radiohead fan, but I do like their music. OK Computer is an briliant CD, like what everyone said. Too bad they don't get much radio time down here. Everyonce in a while I'll hear Karma Police on the radio, and there's always lots and lots of people calling in asking what and who that was. The song before KP (can't remember the name) is awesome too.||||reg||1
Z||000009||AkursedX||06-08-2001||05:49 PM||||I think that OK computer was a great cd, there is no doubt about that, but I thought Pablo Honey and Kid A were just as good.  Hell, even the Bends was great.  I honestly couldn't pick a favorite out of those.  What I like about them is that they are all unique in their own ways, and I can understand why somebody would absolutley love OK Computer but not Kid A.  They are too different, and they really can't even be compared to one another, which is why I like Radiohead so much.  Maybe I'll go buy the new one with my next unemployment check.<P>Oh and by the way, yes I understood what eric said, just never looked at the thread again until now.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Eric||06-08-2001||08:15 PM||||I love The Bends too.  How would you rate Pablo Honey against OK Computer and The Bends.  Obviously, I like the song "Creep", but haven't heard much else from the CD.<P>I listened to Kid A in it's entirety, and I didn't like it.  I was hoping this new one was more like the old, but I guess it's not.||||reg||1
Z||000011||ChadMan||06-08-2001||11:26 PM||||I like Pablo Honey and I think it's worth buying, but it's a pretty ordinary rock album.  Listening to it, there's little indication that The Bends would be so groundbreaking and original, and that OK Computer would be even more groundbreaking.<P>AkursedX, maybe the problem is me and not Kid A/Amnesiac.  Maybe Radiohead has gone somewhere I'm not ready to go yet.<P>I'll fess up...I thought OK Computer was a brilliant expression of how our whole society is teetering on the brink of insanity.  Drug abuse, shooting, road rage...these are SYMPTOMS of a deeper sickness and getting rid of drugs, guns and cars won't make the sickness go away.  Maybe Kid A takes us over the brink into the insanity and I'm not capable of understanding it yet because I'm still sane?<P>(I'm not saying you're crazy, AkursedX...)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||3
Z||000012||AkursedX||06-09-2001||03:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ChadMan:<BR><B><P>(I'm not saying you're crazy, AkursedX...)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>lol, well....you wouldn't be the 1st one to call me that.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <P>The thing about Kid A, is that I think it is way too far ahead of it's time to be truly appreciated.  The music of it is just way too far out there, which is why I love it!  It seems like that cd could bring out an entirely new genre of music.<BR>||||reg||1
